er be/get used to, not after past-habit used to.","D":"Used to already marks the past habit; the following verb stays in the base form."}}},{"id":"4f8bc461-df22-575c-a54a-51c28f5edf60","topicSlug":"past-habits","level":"B1","prompt":"Use did in the negative: I did not ____ the garden fence in my old job.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"use to measuring"},{"id":"B","text":"using to measure"},{"id":"C","text":"use to measure"},{"id":"D","text":"used to measure"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The past marker is already on **did**.","explanation":"After **did not**, standard written English uses **use to measure**.","keywords":["habit-negative"],"skill":"habit-negative","contextKey":"past-habits-3","fingerprint":"5d2163802d79dcd1d0ae13222aea635f8221ae3dfddf1d9bfa2e5d3601181eab","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-habits"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The past marker is already on **did**.","After **did not**, standard written English uses **use to measure**.","Choose **use to measure**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Past-habit use to takes the base verb.","B":"Did requires the base form use, not using.","C":"After **did not**, standard written English uses **use to measure**.","D":"After did, the recommended standard written form is use to, without -d."}}},{"id":"eed80942-093d-55df-a576-529304ee730c","topicSlug":"past-habits","level":"B1","prompt":"I am familiar with the task: I am used to ____ the garden fence.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"measured"},{"id":"B","text":"to measure"},{"id":"C","text":"measuring"},{"id":"D","text":"measure"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"The word **am** changes the construction: this is familiarity, not a former habit.","explanation":"In **am used to**, to is a preposition, so the following verb is **measuring**.","keywords":["accustomed-state"],"skill":"accustomed-state","contextKey":"past-habits-3","fingerprint":"52a07007b0173e70ccd6abbae6a07b9c68de43875f86578f743943e0bf7aace5","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-habits"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The word **am** changes the construction: this is familiarity, not a former habit.","In **am used to**, to is a preposition, so the following verb is **measuring**.","Choose **measuring**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"A past participle does not name the activity after this preposition.","B":"Do not put a to-infinitive after the preposition to in this pattern.","C":"In **am used to**, to is a preposition, so the following verb is **measuring**.","D":"The base verb belongs in the former-habit pattern, not after am used to."}}},{"id":"4b381185-ed79-5e9c-a1fc-a52ef24e3609","topicSlug":"past-habits","level":"B1","prompt":"Recall a repeated action with would: In my old job, I would ____ the garden fence every week.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"measuring"},{"id":"B","text":"measured"},{"id":"C","text":"to measure"},{"id":"D","text":"measure"}],"answerId":"D","hint":"The context supplies a past routine; **would** still takes the base form.","explanation":"Would takes the base verb **measure**. The old job and every week establish a repeated past action.","keywords":["repeated-past-action"],"skill":"repeated-past-action","contextKey":"past-habits-3","fingerprint":"4a5f2a9e9890b0ce5235a2bac24cb615af6f8d52884de3f61b49128c92d2c934","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-habits"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The context supplies a past routine; **would** still takes the base form.","Would takes the base verb **measure**. The old job and every week establish a repeated past action.","Choose **measure**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Would alone cannot take an -ing form.","B":"Would takes a base verb, not a past form.","C":"Would takes a bare infinitive without to.","D":"Would takes the base verb **measure**. The old job and every week establish a repeated past action."}}},{"id":"92711531-8734-5162-a128-8b86f6baa16b","topicSlug":"past-habits","level":"B1","prompt":"Complete a former habit: I used to ____ the travel leaflet, but I do not do that now.","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"translated"},{"id":"B","text":"to translate"},{"id":"C","text":"translate"},{"id":"D","text":"translating"}],"answerId":"C","hint":"Here used to contrasts a past routine with now.","explanation":"The discontinued-habit pattern is **used to + translate**, using the base verb.","keywords":["former-habit"],"skill":"former-habit","contextKey":"past-habits-4","fingerprint":"45178f2e34f47e230d6b8ce7b803433cf3e0a2a69fba4ea8e285593113f52839","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-past-habits"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["Here used to contrasts a past routine with now.","The discontinued-habit pattern is **used to + translate**, using the base verb.","Choose **translate**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"Used to already marks the past habit; the following verb stays in the base form.","B":"To is already present; do not repeat it.","C":"The discontinued-habit pattern is **used to + translate**, using the base verb.","D":"The -ing form belongs after be/get used to, not after past-habit used to."}}},{"id":"6208dc13-bf1a-5bdc-af38-43ef400a685d","topicSlug":"past-habits","level":"B1","prompt":"Use did in the negative: I did not ____ the travel leaflet in